Dark ambient post-rock hypnotic with deep vocal integration;  
melancholic, slow-burning, emotionally resonant — not aggressive, but **profoundly wounded**;  
clean electric bass guitar — sparse, single-note arpeggios in E minor, played with fingerpicking, **soft sustain, slight natural reverb**, like echoes in an empty cathedral;  
melodic bassline — warm analog tone, **long decay, slightly detuned**, playing slow, descending chords (E–C–B–A), **not rhythm-driven, but mournful**, like a cello bow dragged over broken strings;  
analog drum machine — kick (deep, sub-60Hz, felt more than heard), snare (dry, clothed, barely there), closed hi-hat (only on 2nd and 4th beat, 92 BPM), **humanized timing — imperfect, breathing**, like a tired heartbeat;  
synth pad — Juno-106-style, **low-passed to 150Hz**, **slow LFO modulation (0.1 Hz)**, creating a **warm, pulsing bed of air**, not sound — **felt in the ribs**, not the ears;  
no distortion on instruments — **everything is soft, warm, slightly out of tune**, as if played on instruments left in a damp basement for 20 years;  
urban night atmosphere: distant traffic (mono, low-passed at 1kHz), steady rain (stereo, high-passed at 200Hz), subtle wind through metal grates;  
sound texture: analog warmth, light tape hiss, **no compression on master**, **dynamic space preserved**, **midrange (300–800Hz) left wide open** for the voice;  
