Slow-burn psychedelic ambient / neo-psychedelia instrumental;  
dreamlike, hazy, yet emotionally heavy — like walking through rain at 3 a.m. with no destination;  
no rock guitars — instead:  
• layered analog synth pads (Roland Juno, Prophet-5) — slow LFO modulation, drifting phasing, evolving over minutes, tuned to E minor with subtle microtonal detuning;  
• warm, sub-heavy bassline — Moog-style, playing long sustained notes with slow pitch bends, felt more than heard, pulsing at 45 BPM (half-time feel), creating a slow respiratory rhythm;  
• sparse, hypnotic percussion — analog drum machine (LinnDrum or CR-78 style), only kick (sub-heavy, 50Hz) and brushed snare (felt, distant), no hi-hats, no cymbals, tempo ~92 BPM but with **elastic timing**, as if floating in water;  
• tape echo loops — reversed guitar swells (no chords, no notes — just feedback-shaped textures), drenched in spring reverb, panned wide, appearing and vanishing like memories;  
• urban field recordings: rain on metal, distant sirens, muffled traffic — processed through low-pass filters, embedded in stereo field like ghosts in the fog;  
• no sharp attacks — everything swells in and out, like breath;  
• harmony: modal, ambiguous — E minor with added 9ths and suspended 4ths, but blurred by analog drift;  
• mix: ultra-wet (spring reverb, tape delay), but **voice remains dry and central** — as if the singe

Modern hypnotic psychedelic;  
94 BPM; no intro; male vocal from first beat;  

• bass: analog, liquid, E0–A1, tight envelope, slight overdrive, locks with kick;  
• drum machine: kick (sub-heavy), snare (crack, dry), closed hi-hat on offbeats — humanized, no cymbals;  
• synth: Roland Juno-style arpeggio (E minor, 16th notes), stereo phaser, low-pass filtered to 600Hz, constant swirl;  
• atmosphere: light tape hiss, distant rain, embedded as texture;  
• vocal: **MANDATORY — male, deep baritone (G2–E2), raw, throaty, full vocal fry, dry, close-mic, no reverb, no harmonies, no female voices**;  
• vocal enters at beat 1 — no lead-in, no instrumental intro;  
• mix: voice central and dominant in 250–600Hz; synths wide but low; bass and kick mono, physical;  
• no long pauses — space used for breath, not silence;  
• outro: vocal “signal” echoes in analog tape delay, synth rises slightly, then cuts abruptly.

1990s-inspired alternative rock instrumental;  
melancholic yet propulsive, with restrained emotional depth and forward motion;  
clean electric guitar — tight eighth-note arpeggios in E minor, dry amp tone, zero reverb, no sustain, occasional distorted stabs (palm-muted, 150ms decay);  
driving melodic bassline — warm analog tone, slightly overdriven, slow decay, root-note emphasis with occasional chromatic descents, panned slightly left;  
analog drum machine — kick (tight, sub-heavy), snare (dry, wooden crack), closed hi-hat (steady 16ths), 92 BPM, humanized timing (±12ms jitter), no cymbals, no fills, mechanical but with subtle imperfections;  
Roland Juno-106-style synth — low-pass filtered to 200Hz, ultra-subtle pulse (LFO 0.3 Hz), used as atmospheric bed, not melody — felt in the chest, not heard in the ears;  
repetitive, hypnotic groove with no climax, no resolution, no release — the music never "arrives," only persists;  
urban night atmosphere: distant traffic (mono, low-passed at 1kHz), wet pavement, steady rain (stereo, high-passed at 200Hz);  
sound texture: analog warmth, light tape saturation, dry mix, raw and alive — as if recorded on a Tascam 4-track in a basement after midnight;  
dynamic range preserved — no loudness war, no compression on master — let the silence breathe;  
space is left in midrange (400–800Hz) to accommodate the raw, gravelly male vocal —

