mechanical, heavy, with deep sub-bass and minimal harmonic motion — designed to frame a brutal, low, growling male voice;  
clean electric guitar — sparse, single-note arpeggios in E minor, heavily compressed and low-passed to 400Hz, no sustain, played through a distorted tube preamp for grit;  
sub-bass drone — analog synthesizer (Moog-style), 40–60Hz, constant, creates physical pressure in chest — never louder than the voice, but always present;  
analog drum machine — kick (sub-heavy, 60Hz), snare (dry, wooden, barely audible), closed hi-hat (occasional, 8th notes), 92 BPM, humanized timing (±10ms jitter), no cymbals, no fills, sparse, like a failing heartbeat;  
minimal analog synth pad — Juno-style, low-pass filtered to 180Hz, barely there, creates tension without competing for space;  
no lead melodies — only rhythm and sub-pressure;  
repetitive, hypnotic groove with no climax, no resolution — just persistence;  
urban night atmosphere: distant traffic (mono, low-passed at 1kHz), wet pavement, steady rain (stereo, high-passed at 200Hz);  
sound texture: raw, analog warmth, tape compression, dry mix — no reverb on instruments, only on vocals;  
dynamic range preserved — space left in 100–400Hz for the brutal, chest-driven vocals;  
