Cinematic dark ambient / slow psychedelic instrumental;  
voice-centric, minimalist, sub-heavy;  
no traditional instruments — only textures, drones, and field recordings;  

• sub-bass drone — Moog-style analog oscillator, 38–42Hz, ultra-slow LFO (0.05 Hz), creates physical pressure, never exceeds -18dB;  
• ambient bed — layered tape loops of distant city noise, processed through broken reel-to-reel (wow/flutter +3%), low-passed to 150Hz, panned wide;  
• analog synth pads — Juno-60 and Prophet-5, detuned, playing single sustained chords (E minor add9), filtered to 120Hz, evolving over 4+ minutes;  
• sparse percussion — only one element: a reversed heartbeat sample (from vinyl crackle), played every 8 bars, drenched in spring reverb, then abruptly cut;  
• tempo: none. Pulse only — implied by sub-bass swells at 48 BPM (felt, not counted);  
• no melodies, no arpeggios, no chords in high register — everything lives below 300Hz;  
• urban atmosphere: rain on concrete, distant subway rumble, flickering neon transformer buzz — all embedded as harmonic texture;  
• mix: extremely dry on vocal channel; everything else — wet (spring reverb, tape delay), creating a “dry island in a wet void” effect;  
• dynamic range preserved — no limiting, no loudness war;  
• frequency space: 250–600Hz left wide open for the voice’s core resonance — the only place where “human” exists;  
