1999 alternative rock song, recorded at The Mansion studio, produced by Rick Rubin;
male tenor vocal: breathy, slightly nasal, conversational, recorded on Neumann U47, 15cm distance, no pop filter;
vocal processing: LA-2A compression (2:1 ratio), no reverb in verses, EMT 140 plate reverb (1.1s decay) only in chorus;
double-tracked vocals in chorus: main center, harmony -5 semitones panned left;
guitar: Fender Stratocaster, played with fingers, clean tone, Fender Deluxe Reverb amp (volume 4), Roland CE-1 analog chorus;
bass: 1960s Fender Precision Bass, flatwound strings, fingerstyle, slight tube overdrive, no effects, panned center;
drums: Ludwig kit, coated Ambassador snare, felt beater on kick, no cymbals, close-mic only (no room mics), 92 BPM;
arrangement: minimal, no synth, no strings, no backing vocals except double-tracked lead;
sound texture: dry mix, natural amp hum, tape saturation (Ampex ATR-102), mono-compatible low end, high frequencies rolled off above 12kHz;

